Match Wine ALSA producer wake correction to its actual QPC clock.

Wine 10 alsa_timer_loop reads NtQueryPerformanceCounter for next/last period
correction. Unix QPC prefers CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW, otherwise CLOCK_MONOTONIC,
and truncates to 100-ns ticks. The old native producer used adjusted MONOTONIC
nanoseconds. Use the same clock selection and tick precision, including Wine's
signed 32-bit difference before its half-period clamp. OS nanosleep and the
virtual/hardware sample clock remain independent. No output, silence or
presentation offset is fitted; complete movie A/V parity remains unproven.

Primary sources:
https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/wine-10.0/dlls/winealsa.drv/alsa.c
https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/wine-10.0/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c

--- a/dd2_native_movie_alsa.h
+++ b/dd2_native_movie_alsa.h
@@ -93,23 +93,33 @@
